From 9cfe17f65eb4c573a1d2eb3a26abfe359218ddfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: readmet3xt-lab <238408149+readmet3xt-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:25:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 79/81] VICTORY_AMBIENT_ONCE: the lighting stand-in without its
 own light fed back

The stand-in raises the diffuse light to an estimate made from the light the
visible surfaces sent out the frame before, which it had raised itself: its
own light comes back to it reflected, and the light settles at
level*e/(1 - level*a) rather than one bounce (1.3x at walls that send out
0.6, 1.75x at 0.9; more near lamps and pale walls: the overexposed rooms;
R3: VICTORY_AMBIENT=0 is much darker, lamps less blown).

With VICTORY_AMBIENT_ONCE=1 the raise notes, at the 25 places of each cell
the next keep reads, the share of the light there that is the title's own,
and the keep counts each place's light by that share: one bounce of the
title's light. Off by default (an A/B first). Light surfaces make
themselves (lamps) is counted down too where the stand-in raised it
(shortcut: no albedo to tell them apart). The cells' buffer grows by 25
entries a cell (0.9 MB).

Test: a model of keep and raise over frames (fed back vs once), and the
passes still build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8cf0a752675d7e6a12ef46fb824f3179ce5a9054)
